# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file requests a review from the listed owners on any pull request
# touching a matching path. It does NOT by itself block merging — that
# requires enabling "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch
# protection settings for `main` (currently unset; see the Governance
# Report for the recommended settings).
#
# Design: kept intentionally minimal for the project's current size (two
# maintainers, a handful of collaborators with read-only access, no
# formal sub-teams yet). One blanket rule covers the whole repository;
# a couple of explicit rules exist only to document intent for
# `docs/` and `.github/`, since GitHub gives the *last* matching rule
# priority — right now they're redundant with the wildcard below, but
# they establish the file structure a maintainer can later edit in place
# (e.g. adding `/qrnetwork/network.py @some-physics-lead`) without
# having to redesign the whole file. Students are deliberately not
# listed as owners of any path; add contributors here only once they
# have a standing review responsibility, not merely write access.
#
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default: every file requires review from a maintainer unless a more
# specific rule below says otherwise.
